sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as Browser
  participant W as Next.js server action<br/>layalga_web role
  participant DB as Postgres<br/>runs table
  participant CRON as Vercel Cron<br/>GET /api/ticks
  participant AC as AgentCore Runtime<br/>handleAgentCoreRequest
  participant S as Strands agent loop
  participant M as Bedrock<br/>Sonnet 4.6
  participant T as Typed tools
  participant EMAIL as Web guest delivery<br/>SES adapter

  B->>W: submit form
  W->>DB: startRun: insert status queued<br/>intent_key per home, replay if already seen
  DB-->>W: runId, sessionId
  W-->>B: acknowledgement {status queued, runId}
  Note over W,DB: Queued means accepted work, not a result.<br/>Poll the exact run to a terminal state.

  par Browser polls the run
    loop every 1.5 s until terminal or deadline_at
      B->>W: GET /api/runs/{id}?token
      W->>DB: getAuthorizedRunSnapshot
      DB-->>W: status, events, summary, executedOn
      W-->>B: JSON, cache-control no-store
    end
  and Dispatch of the queued run
    alt AGENT_RUNTIME=agentcore
      W->>AC: InvokeAgentRuntime<br/>{operation execute_run, runId, task}
      AC->>DB: claimQueuedRun: status running, claim token,<br/>attempt +1 (max 3), deadline now + 4 min
      AC-->>W: {status accepted, runId}
    else AGENT_RUNTIME=local
      W->>W: after(): executeQueuedAgentRun in process
      W->>DB: claimQueuedRun (same claim rules)
    else Vercel Cron tick (Bearer CRON_SECRET)
      CRON->>W: GET /api/ticks
      W->>DB: reconcileStaleRuns: deadline passed and attempts < 3<br/>back to queued, else failed
      W->>DB: expireTemporaryHolds
      W->>DB: claimDueJob: scheduled_jobs due, 10 min lease
      W->>DB: enqueue tick run per due job, not opportunistic
      W->>DB: drainAgentQueue: queued or stale running (6 min),<br/>attempts < 3, concurrency 2
      W->>AC: InvokeAgentRuntime execute_run per candidate
      AC->>DB: claimQueuedRun
      AC-->>W: {status accepted}
      W->>W: dispatchHostEmailPingsSafely
      W->>EMAIL: dispatchGuestEmailPingsSafely<br/>real clock, synthetic homes excluded
      EMAIL->>DB: claim source + contact generation with lease
      EMAIL->>DB: under home lock recheck consent, access,<br/>current visit/job cycle and prearrival,<br/>persist authorized attempt
      EMAIL->>EMAIL: send through SES outside transaction
      EMAIL->>DB: persist provider acceptance independently<br/>of later cancellation or opt-out
      Note over EMAIL,DB: Unresolved authorized attempt becomes unknown,<br/>never blindly resend. Acceptance is not inbox delivery.
    end

    AC->>S: agent.invoke(prompt), 240 s budget<br/>session stored in agent_sessions
    loop model and tool turns
      S->>M: converse
      M-->>S: text or tool use
      S->>T: tool call, policy hook first for gated tools
      T->>DB: read, or authorized write, plus audit row
      T-->>S: tool result
    end
    S-->>AC: completed, interrupted, or failed
    AC->>DB: terminal result {summary, executedOn}<br/>claim token cleared, finished_at set
  end

  B->>B: poller renders timeline<br/>tool_call, policy_verdict, decision_applied
  opt Newly captured invitation, exact run completed
    B->>W: authorized POST revealCapturedInvitationAction<br/>one automatic attempt, explicit retry after failure
    W->>DB: verify current host, home and completed capture run
    W-->>B: private link in action result only
  end
  opt Guest enables reminders on a real invitation
    B->>W: explicit consent POST, typed address or verified Google identity
    W->>DB: scoped contact generation and verification outbox
    Note over B,DB: Account-free GET only previews verification,<br/>explicit POST verifies. Return capability is checked<br/>against live access and consent on every guest request.
  end
  Note over B: After deadline_at the poller stops<br/>and shows a Retry status button.
